				{
					"id": "EEaIYEHFWcv0SJJtK",
					"description": "Common Bucklers",
					"local_notes": "Any shield wielded with a central handgrip is a buckler. You can ready it in one second and drop it as a free action. \n\nThe Basic Set states that a buckler can’t be used for a shield rush (p. B406). This isn’t quite true; the Roman scutum was specifically designed for this tactic. However, it is difficult to put your full weight behind a buckler – damage is at -1, relative to a shield, in a rush",
